# Every variable this gateway reads, and only those. The two with no default
# are the two it refuses to start without: each names something it cannot
# function without — somewhere to reach, or the name it answers to — and
# defaulting either produces a process that starts, answers /health, and does
# nothing it exists to do.
#
# Both are read only where RailXia is installed, so a gateway with
# RAIL_PLUGIN_ENABLED unset starts on its routes file alone.

# Where the upstreams this gateway fronts are named: one file, `mcp.servers`,
# an entry per upstream with `name`, `url` and an optional `prefix`. Required
# in every mode — a gateway fronting nothing forwards nothing. Defaults to
# /etc/rail/routes.yaml, which the image bakes and does not ship, so a
# container started without one mounted stops rather than coming up empty.
RAIL_GATEWAY_ROUTES_FILE=

# Where the policy bundle comes from. Required when RAIL_PLUGIN_ENABLED is
# true, and not read at all when it is false — a plain gateway fetches no
# bundle. Setting it with the plugin off is refused at startup, naming both. The route beneath it is the
# OpenAPI specification's, so what a deployment configures is the origin alone.
RAIL_CENTER_URL=

# Which gateway this is, and whose policy bundle it fetches. Required where the
# plugin is enabled. **Not a data source's slug**: a gateway fronts several data
# sources and a data source may sit behind several gateways, so no data source
# can name the component. Rail Center builds the bundle for this gateway —
# its bindings, its posture, its fallback.
RAIL_GATEWAY_SLUG=

# Whether RailXia is installed on this deployment: true | false. Default false,
# so a plain gateway needs no variable at all. A deployment carrying Rail Center
# configuration with this off is refused at startup naming both, which is what
# keeps that default from silently unenrolling a gateway that was enforcing.
# Platform-wide rather than this component's own — the proxy in front reads the
# same question — so case is folded and one value configures a whole zone.
#
# It does NOT say how much of a decision is acted on. That is the bundle's
# `enforcement` posture, and it arrives on every poll, so moving a gateway
# between judging nothing, reporting and refusing is a change in Rail Center
# rather than a redeploy. A deployment still setting RAIL_TICKET_MODE is refused
# at startup, with a message naming this variable and the bundle.
RAIL_PLUGIN_ENABLED=

# The credential presented to Rail Center: none | bearer. `gcp` is named by the
# platform contract and refused by this component under its own name rather
# than as an unknown mode. RAIL_AUTH_TOKEN is required when the mode is bearer
# and unread otherwise.
RAIL_AUTH_MODE=
RAIL_AUTH_TOKEN=

# How often to ask Rail Center for the bundle again, in seconds. Default 60,
# floor 5 — a value below the floor is raised to it with a warning rather than
# refused, since an interval that is merely too eager is not worth taking
# enforcement down over.
RAIL_GATEWAY_BUNDLE_REFRESH_SECONDS=

# Default 8080.
RAIL_GATEWAY_PORT=

# CRITICAL | ERROR | WARNING | INFO | DEBUG. Default INFO.
RAIL_GATEWAY_LOG_LEVEL=
